#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1020.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120580} :activity/id #uuid "2660cd04-6f2d-5dd7-95c2-55cf96cdbf95" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049196 :topic/id #uuid "e289a183-5534-5388-8ee7-3fc0d8f4ee68" :topic/math-academy-id 1833} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120580 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121002 :tutorial/content "The **curvature** of a curve measures how much the curve \"bends\" at a given point. It can also be thought of as a measure of how much the curve deviates from being a straight line. Curvature is denoted by the Greek letter $\\kappa$ (pronounced \"kappa\"). \n\nIf $\\kappa=0$ at some point on a curve, then that curve looks like a straight line in some neighborhood of the point.\n\nIf the curve $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ is parametrized by the arc length $s,$ then the curvature $\\kappa$ is the magnitude of the change of direction of the unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T$ per unit of arc length. That is,\n\n$$\n\\kappa(s) = \\left\\| \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf T}{\\textrm{d}s}  \\right\\|= \\| \\mathbf T'(s) \\|.\n$$\n\nNote that $|| \\mathbf v ||$ denotes the magnitude of the vector $\\mathbf v.$\n\nFor example, suppose we are given the curve \n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(s)= \\left\\langle \\sin\\left(\\dfrac s2\\right), \\: \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2}, \\: -\\cos\\left(\\dfrac s2\\right)\\right\\rangle\n$$\n\n \nwhich is parametrized by arc length $s.$ Let's find the curvature of  $\\mathbf r(s)$  at the point where $s={\\pi}.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit tangent vector:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) =\\dfrac 12 \\left\\langle \\cos\\left( \\dfrac s2\\right), \\: \\sqrt{3}, \\: \\sin \\left(\\dfrac s2\\right)\\right\\rangle\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we differentiate $\\mathbf{T}(s)$ and evaluate its absolute value at $s=\\pi\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature by taking the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\pi ) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\pi )‖=\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n**Note:** To calculate $\\kappa,$ the function $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ should be at least twice differentiable with respect to $s.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "d74577d5-5fe6-5544-bd86-b20fee42defa" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2402 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "12125b22-92e2-567c-9dc7-87e721cb0430" :step/math-academy-id 10650 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120581}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120581 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119748 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119564 :question/id #uuid "219df52e-8833-58df-8a2f-ee53cfed5640" :question/math-academy-id "e-3135"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9befd973-a2d9-567a-8808-d126ecaaae1b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048999} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051021}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120316} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120494} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317323} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335730} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348420} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351527} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351528} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443896} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443897} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443901} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443902}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization And the Unit Tangent"} :step/id #uuid "9b2d3984-cd37-5bc8-b3ce-f427ae5bd607" :step/math-academy-id 10651 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120583}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120582 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119749 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119565 :question/id #uuid "ea963bd4-6c5b-5385-8efc-dcd4de104da0" :question/math-academy-id "e-3140"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c9d719f-4936-5994-90eb-c33da57639cc" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050685}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120299} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120305} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266064} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266065} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317268} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335731} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335732} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335734} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348422} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351529} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375923} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411868} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433629} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433630} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443899} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480641} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497416}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given a General Parametrization"} :step/id #uuid "cd83eef1-8999-5702-814d-b4f011d666e1" :step/math-academy-id 10657} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120583 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119750 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119566 :question/id #uuid "2db0218f-bfb3-552a-8683-2f32f230a3ca" :question/math-academy-id "e-3141"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120326} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120495} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266122} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266123} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268874} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317250} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348404} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348411} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351524} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375930} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375937} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377777} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443898} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443900} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443903}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization"} :step/id #uuid "3a00b3b6-447c-5ccc-97a8-7cd65929b702" :step/math-academy-id 10658 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120594}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120594 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121007 :tutorial/content "If the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ is parametrized by a general parameter $t,$ then\n\n$$\n\\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\|\\mathbf T'(t)\\|}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|}.\n$$\n\nTo understand why this is, remember that the arc length $s$ and the parameter $t$ are related by the formula \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle s(t)= \\int_0^t\\left\\| \\mathbf  r'(x)\\right\\|\\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nBy the chain rule and the fundamental theorem of calculus, then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d  \\mathbf T}{\\textrm d t} = \\dfrac{\\textrm d  \\mathbf T}{\\textrm d s} \\dfrac{\\textrm d  s}{\\textrm d t}= \\dfrac{\\textrm d  \\mathbf T}{\\textrm d s} \\left\\| \\mathbf r'(t)\\right\\|.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}‖ & =‖\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}s}‖‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =κ(t)‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ \\\\ κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "a3b41506-4cd1-5589-b3a6-4cd3f4ecbdb2" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2484 :tutorial/title "The Curvature of Curves Parametrized Using a General Parameter"} :step/id #uuid "d9dd47a2-479b-5929-a71d-4ad46370bfb7" :step/math-academy-id 11099 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120582}}] :activity/title "Introduction to Curvature" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186120033}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433631} :activity/id #uuid "2b8eb350-78af-5600-9e7a-328caccbfa84" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049196 :topic/id #uuid "e289a183-5534-5388-8ee7-3fc0d8f4ee68" :topic/math-academy-id 1833} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433631 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433630 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1367431b-f708-53d0-907c-401baf44b1b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433618} {:answer/id #uuid "5ddff454-cafc-5d0a-8e73-761ad50a723b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{{(8{t}^{2}+2)}^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433620} {:answer/id #uuid "ae9b1f32-4af7-5ccc-b6f9-f8acc59e69d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433621} {:answer/id #uuid "e1ed4446-c062-507c-a44a-cf42f43f3e0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433624} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cd5e7a-fd43-5ce4-9986-155332afc1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433626}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433621} :answer-field/id #uuid "c90f0f81-e6f6-5365-9a31-9800a129aea5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d3e668b2-3360-5bad-970e-ebd786d68368" :question/math-academy-id "q-64696" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t.$ Since we are given the curve $r(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+2t\\,j+1\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nHence, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}}(2t\\,i+2t\\,j+k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}})\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}(2\\,i+2\\,j-8t\\,k) \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-8t)^{2}}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8+{8}^{2}{t}^{2}}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8(1+8{t}^{2})}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8}\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{8}\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}})}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "00d70dc7-07a1-5030-82b3-0ddd637fbfb1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433632}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433632 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120495 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0c9c1f0-df55-556e-833a-7fb64732dde4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119085} {:answer/id #uuid "f30dc2a4-65fc-5750-b501-c7c5b426ccda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119086} {:answer/id #uuid "092a0aaf-082d-545c-9806-110ce43d35b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119087} {:answer/id #uuid "3ef17328-d207-5798-8681-f24753e09c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119088} {:answer/id #uuid "62750844-6757-5328-89ca-54678ebfa45e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119089}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119087} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ccd57a8-0a01-50d0-ac4b-6f5f8f6b6e44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4163ce17-8c2e-5e7a-b5d2-d7191ad32de0" :question/math-academy-id "q-64700" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩,\\,0\\le s<2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}+{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)}^{2}+{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡s+\\frac{1}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡s+\\frac{1}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡s+{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "59cb16be-b5c6-5ba7-9b02-4ee7270ded13" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433633}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433633 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433629 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1251bed4-415d-5590-a871-e4a9657e13d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433617} {:answer/id #uuid "481e6b9f-c5af-58b8-b98e-c12965a43b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433619} {:answer/id #uuid "c86e68ce-7275-5906-ac2f-57213bf72bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433622} {:answer/id #uuid "d87a76ef-7c66-5822-bbbd-0695f641dc2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433623} {:answer/id #uuid "e5a5693f-64fa-5920-9519-f34d893234c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433625}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433622} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ef00e22-7033-5539-a4d7-5c70d771c4f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c48a3e25-1a31-5723-bb94-d587dcc4bb55" :question/math-academy-id "q-80546" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${T}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))}^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2t))} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2 \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)+16{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡(2t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(2t))} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\,2\\,}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "cb9b8003-d330-530b-a31a-213d60c41132"}] :activity/title "Introduction to Curvature" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433616}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480716} :activity/id #uuid "838f800d-4d4e-5cfd-a81a-a2e2c5e265e9" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049196 :topic/id #uuid "e289a183-5534-5388-8ee7-3fc0d8f4ee68" :topic/math-academy-id 1833} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480714 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c819a8-69c1-5f0d-ba40-eb78fd2be723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377779} {:answer/id #uuid "39f59b00-cc03-55ab-b6b8-1ab9c1ffeae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377780} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a6473f-4085-5582-85ae-4516ab8e6591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377781} {:answer/id #uuid "f7652fff-4d92-5f23-894d-77bffbcfe791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377782} {:answer/id #uuid "6fa70a7e-2036-5502-bde5-0309ee363352" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377783}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377782} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0a1617d-d91d-575d-bb6f-36a897794ae3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "729c5739-583c-5a71-86c4-2b95ece46c63" :question/math-academy-id "q-80615" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where:\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{3s+1}{5},\\,\\frac{3-4s}{5}⟩,\\,s\\ge 0\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3s+1}{5}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3-4s}{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{5},\\,-\\frac{4}{5}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3}{5}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{4}{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "173d0f58-bc34-562c-946e-5bc2263093ae" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480726}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480716 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335732 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37af32ac-6d56-59b7-af88-a83bd549c119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333502} {:answer/id #uuid "89b6e43c-5175-58b9-a703-c4d3bd3ea434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334213} {:answer/id #uuid "ec91d17d-8a59-5d87-b344-af638420e8b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335062} {:answer/id #uuid "f164ca79-a714-5ace-a91e-f41a09d97456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335104} {:answer/id #uuid "fd455317-5a16-56c0-bbb9-11acb365385d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335216}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335062} :answer-field/id #uuid "91f964f4-328c-5d44-bbab-649563165d63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fe9f4359-a5d3-51ab-bfaf-67dd4916cffb" :question/math-academy-id "q-64666" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{2}\\,i-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{2})}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{2}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "291516b6-6940-55a8-a9ef-96c84649e02e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480725}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480723 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480641 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "080f6753-8c70-5915-9a0d-bd865b290678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480125} {:answer/id #uuid "6cdb4830-f175-5239-a293-3eeaeb64ec02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{t}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480286} {:answer/id #uuid "79a108d2-31f6-5580-a65c-9af14c23117c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480310} {:answer/id #uuid "9ce60844-2f9b-561b-af0b-96198d74c1e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{-t}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480369} {:answer/id #uuid "cebd021e-80fb-5feb-a087-fc29f42f4665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480457}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480369} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbef7b1b-2a5f-5dce-929c-f5b8a633c936" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1fed5aa4-7f90-50cb-8379-da324cfd5754" :question/math-academy-id "q-80612" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)={e}^{t}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t),$ we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${T}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =|-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sqrt{({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sqrt{1+1+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =1 \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{1+1+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{t}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{-t}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9e6ecfea-3213-5f5e-8c4a-e8863d69e102" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480714}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480725 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4803543c-d61e-5f5c-968e-bc681feef549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-2s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345969} {:answer/id #uuid "4ca68699-5d12-50bb-b538-dd82a35e755d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346010} {:answer/id #uuid "724bf20d-270c-5376-b989-0685a8f99019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2s(1-2s)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346362} {:answer/id #uuid "7f95752a-9af9-56bd-b358-ebcec0812d80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2s(1-2s)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346470} {:answer/id #uuid "fd88f132-9956-5edd-b9a1-d15e9c7f24c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347583}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186346362} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8a7def3-c10e-5e3b-9fa8-80d05175b949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "61dc28ce-9be1-5118-b764-acd32225832e" :question/math-academy-id "q-80545" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s,$ where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{1}{3}(1-2s)^{3/2},\\,\\frac{1}{3}(2s)^{3/2}⟩,\\,0<s<\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{1}{3}(1-2s)^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{1}{3}(2s)^{3/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (1-2s)^{1/2}\\cdot (-2),\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (2s)^{1/2}\\cdot 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-(1-2s)^{1/2},\\,(2s)^{1/2}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-(1-2s)^{1/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}((2s)^{1/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (1-2s)^{-1/2}\\cdot (-2),\\,\\frac{1}{2}(2s)^{-1/2}\\cdot 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(1-2s)^{-1/2},\\,(2s)^{-1/2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally, the curvature is  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{((1-2s)^{-1/2})}^{2}+{((2s)^{-1/2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-2s)^{-1}+(2s)^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{1-2s}+\\frac{1}{2s}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2s(1-2s)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e14787e1-3392-5b75-86fb-9d1be487906e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480723}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480726 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3a2b495-5ade-5c9a-9d43-e728c9e4e7f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375932} {:answer/id #uuid "c6b5f8c0-9dbf-52e2-b352-6bda2e491150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375933} {:answer/id #uuid "8e89e463-6ffe-5364-93ab-503d653f6f23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375934} {:answer/id #uuid "7497e593-0737-5859-a271-48d7055fc136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375935} {:answer/id #uuid "a2b1a993-2545-55a0-85bf-22a1c6300847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375936}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375935} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb321e95-8036-5305-85cc-8daac472f444" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "19f64431-6e90-56df-bce1-3e6c04731f56" :question/math-academy-id "q-131930" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,1,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩,\\,0\\le s<2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡s+{cos}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "eadaeefa-26f8-5e0a-8e0b-62d766f44665"}] :activity/title "Introduction to Curvature" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480112}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497429} :activity/id #uuid "4b16e189-7cae-52c7-b4b2-a5ce8c27642e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049196 :topic/id #uuid "e289a183-5534-5388-8ee7-3fc0d8f4ee68" :topic/math-academy-id 1833} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497429 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335734 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0654fbb0-4464-57df-b997-793b4d140585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333048} {:answer/id #uuid "5118678c-2f8f-5690-b6fc-bf8555ce98e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333728} {:answer/id #uuid "7651226e-fce4-5b52-bc1a-76607be7511d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334058} {:answer/id #uuid "7c4a2192-9402-508c-9568-f3777b5cf2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334100} {:answer/id #uuid "a9569df6-5bae-5e8a-824f-b880322a1e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334472}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333728} :answer-field/id #uuid "25483b54-8d2f-5ef1-a991-a9c7271a8af6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b6d968e1-179a-5b9e-896d-829a90d9d8fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-64680" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)=⟨\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,t⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t.$ Since we are given the curve $r(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)}^{2}+{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({cos}^{2}⁡(3t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(3t))+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\sqrt{(9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{2}+(-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\sqrt{{9}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡3t+{cos}^{2}⁡3t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\,\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}\\,}{\\sqrt{10}}=\\frac{9}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "295eca98-5a56-59b6-be3f-1a7e5fc824dc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497462}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497447 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497416 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5063f8a0-899b-5e4f-b70e-5fbeab173e14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496834} {:answer/id #uuid "cf933d00-1cd0-58a3-b054-9a9b5f189803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497086} {:answer/id #uuid "df8562cf-2270-52ce-9299-2a3db48074d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497137} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e14dc5-18ed-5023-8fe2-0751bffc21d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497158} {:answer/id #uuid "fe3568be-b178-5f3b-b7ec-36b1e63a80e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2t}{({t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497204}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497137} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6ba6fef-e5a6-577a-86ab-a507607e574c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f8afba66-d1aa-558e-99f9-1c7592f06bb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-131232" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,2\\sqrt{2}t,\\,4⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}⟨4t,\\,\\sqrt{2}(4-{t}^{2}),\\,-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{(4t)}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2}(4-{t}^{2}))}^{2}+(-4t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{16{t}^{2}+2{(4-{t}^{2})}^{2}+16{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{16{t}^{2}+(32-16{t}^{2}+2{t}^{4})+16{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2{t}^{4}+16{t}^{2}+32} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2({t}^{2}+4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{{t}^{2}+4} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{({t}^{2})}^{2}+{(2\\sqrt{2}t)}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+8{t}^{2}+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{(\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{{t}^{2}+4})}{{t}^{2}+4}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7996da4d-65c7-519a-8f8a-fbfe32a74aa7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497455}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497455 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266122 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eb19a9f-9048-5bd2-9825-48b46c374012" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263819} {:answer/id #uuid "6b1b9851-e23d-5c89-85c7-166c2502e4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263923} {:answer/id #uuid "792aef7e-fcea-560d-8fb8-5bfd5fef2507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264051} {:answer/id #uuid "d64da940-c21b-5ec2-8ac3-b32049952204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264863} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb74e9b-1c1a-510f-8253-e0339f0362f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265089}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265089} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cc15e45-edbf-58cf-997c-64f5fe6f3649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c55df30b-b976-5e8f-92e6-7035630c5b16" :question/math-academy-id "q-131931" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\frac{\\sqrt{5}s}{3}⟩,\\,0\\le s\\le 4\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}s}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-\\frac{1}{3}|\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8c342d34-2861-5edd-8ee3-b1b129ac8611"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497462 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348404 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "099529b2-f2d8-571a-8051-1abe76e80e34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345427} {:answer/id #uuid "1c89dd2c-b2a6-55ce-9cde-64a9db39f22a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345598} {:answer/id #uuid "2af3437a-013c-5c2c-ba66-e91d3d0b3776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345732} {:answer/id #uuid "e08432ed-6cab-5f33-bc9d-ccb5e07f25a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347321} {:answer/id #uuid "e22f899c-983b-59f9-b450-dbd732e6a167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347340}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345732} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5bdbcf-f249-5c99-b7cb-71c1723c6391" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "19bd97de-146f-5b50-9592-8b78d39231d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-80523" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩,\\,0\\le s<10\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5},\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5},\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-\\frac{1}{5}|\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a52d7a0f-ae82-55ee-b781-f303b31787d0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497471}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497471 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433629 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1251bed4-415d-5590-a871-e4a9657e13d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433617} {:answer/id #uuid "481e6b9f-c5af-58b8-b98e-c12965a43b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433619} {:answer/id #uuid "c86e68ce-7275-5906-ac2f-57213bf72bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433622} {:answer/id #uuid "d87a76ef-7c66-5822-bbbd-0695f641dc2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433623} {:answer/id #uuid "e5a5693f-64fa-5920-9519-f34d893234c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433625}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433622} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ef00e22-7033-5539-a4d7-5c70d771c4f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c48a3e25-1a31-5723-bb94-d587dcc4bb55" :question/math-academy-id "q-80546" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${T}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))}^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2t))} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2 \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)+16{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡(2t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(2t))} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\,2\\,}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "bc2db5d0-2c5f-5532-ae92-9e8a5ca14fe2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497447}}] :activity/title "Introduction to Curvature" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496647}]}
